     * 
     * @param pools List of Pool objects to process
     * @return Map containing:
     *         - "count": total number of pools
     *         - "active_pools": list of active pools (excluding special ID "287")
     *         - "special_pools": list of pools with special ID "287"
     *         - "name_length_stats": map with average, max, and min name lengths
     */
    public Map<String, Object> processPoolData(List<Pool> pools) {
        // Implementation goes here
    }

    public static class Pool {
        private String name;
        private String search_id;
        private String image;

        public Pool(String name, String search_id, String image) {
            this.name = name;
            this.search_id = search_id;
            this.image = image;
        }

        public String getName() { return name; }
        public String getSearch_id() { return search_id; }
        public String getImage() { return image; }
    }
}
```

## Method Specifications
1. **processPoolData(List<Pool> pools)**
   - Takes a list of Pool objects as input
   - Returns a Map with the following keys and values:
     - "count": Integer representing the total number of pools
     - "active_pools": List of Pool objects excluding those with search_id "287"
     - "special_pools": List of Pool objects with search_id "287"
     - "name_length_stats": Map containing:
       - "average": Average length of pool names (rounded to nearest integer)
       - "max": Maximum length of pool names
       - "min": Minimum length of pool names

## Constraints
- The Pool class must have exactly the specified fields and methods
- The processPoolData method must return a Map with exactly the specified structure
- All calculations should be case-sensitive
