instruction_history.instruction:
Implement a TicTacToeGame class that initializes an N x N board with '-' characters, where N is provided in the constructor. The game should start with player 'X'. The makeMove method should allow placing 'X' or 'O' on empty cells and alternate turns. You should write self-contained code starting with: ```java
import java.util.ArrayList;
import java.util.List;

class TicTacToeGame {
    private char[][] board;
    private char currentPlayer;

    public TicTacToeGame(int size) {
        this.board = new char[size][size];
        for (int i = 0; i < size; i++) {
            for (int j = 0; j < size; j++) {
                board[i][j] = '-';
            }
        }
        this.currentPlayer = 'X';
    }

    public boolean makeMove(int row, int col) {
        if (board[row][col] != '-') return false;
        board[row][col] = currentPlayer;
        currentPlayer = (currentPlayer == 'X') ? 'O' : 'X';
        return true;
    }

    public List<String> getBoardState() {
        List<String> state = new ArrayList<>();
        for (char[] row : board) {
            state.add(new String(row));
        }
        return state;
    }

    public char getCurrentPlayer() {
        return currentPlayer;
    }
}
```

