List<Integer> result = LinkedListSwapper.linkedListToList(swapped);
// result will be [30, 20, 10]
```

### Example 3: Invalid Swap
```java
List<Integer> elements = Arrays.asList(5, 8, 12);
LinkedListNode<Integer> head = LinkedListSwapper.createLinkedList(elements);
LinkedListNode<Integer> swapped = LinkedListSwapper.swapNodes(head, 1, 5);
List<Integer> result = LinkedListSwapper.linkedListToList(swapped);
// result will be [5, 8, 12] (unchanged)
```

## Notes
- Your implementation must exactly match the specified class and method signatures
- The helper methods (createLinkedList and linkedListToList) will be used for testing
- Do not modify the node class definition
- Focus on handling all edge cases in the swapNodes method

