Implement a basic product management system with a Product class and an EnhancedProductManager class. The EnhancedProductManager should store products in a map and support adding and retrieving products. The addProduct method should return a map with 'status' and 'message' keys indicating success. You should write self-contained code starting with: ```java
import java.util.*;

class EnhancedProductManager {
    private Map<Integer, Product> productDatabase;

    public EnhancedProductManager() {
        this.productDatabase = new HashMap<>();
    }

    public Map<String, String> addProduct(Product product) {
        Map<String, String> result = new HashMap<>();
        if (product == null) {
            result.put("status", "error");
            result.put("message", "Product cannot be null");
            return result;
        }
        productDatabase.put(product.getId(), product);
        result.put("status", "success");
        result.put("message", "Product added successfully");
        return result;
    }

    public List<Product> getAllProducts() {
        return new ArrayList<>(productDatabase.values());
    }
}

class Product {
    private int id;
    private String name;
    private int categoryId;

