// Returns: ["|READ", "|WRITE", "|EXECUTE", "|DELETE"]

// Example 2: Single non-exclusive flag
Set<String> result2 = processor.processFlags("EXECUTE");
// Returns: ["EXECUTE|READ", "EXECUTE|WRITE", "EXECUTE|DELETE"]

// Example 3: Invalid combination
processor.processFlags("READ|WRITE");
// Throws IllegalArgumentException
```

## Notes

- Your implementation must exactly match the class structure and method signatures shown
- You may assume all inputs to the constructor are non-null
- The returned set should not contain duplicate combinations
- The order of flags in the output strings doesn't matter
- Mutual exclusivity only applies to flags that are in the exclusive groups set

