Round 3: Ensure that when extending the bitset, any newly allocated words in the `long[]` array are properly initialized to zero, and that 'ghost' bits beyond the original `numBits` are not exposed with garbage values, relying on safe array growth that clears unused positions.

records.current_solution:
public static FixedBitSet ensureCapacity(FixedBitSet bits, int numBits) {
    if (numBits < bits.numBits) {
        return bits;
    } else {
        int numWords = bits2words(numBits);
        long[] arr = bits.getBits();
        if (numWords > arr.length) {
            int oldLength = arr.length;
            arr = ArrayUtil.grow(arr, numWords + 1);
            // Clear newly allocated words to ensure ghost bits are zero
            for (int i = oldLength; i < arr.length; i++) {
                arr[i] = 0L;
            }
        }
        return new FixedBitSet(arr, arr.length << 6);
    }
}

