public void retain(Bits selected) {
    // Your code here
}```

Round 2: Ensure the method does not use any additional array or data structure for storage; perform the element retention in-place by shifting elements forward within the existing arrays. Optimize the implementation to avoid unnecessary element assignments when the read and write indices are the same, i.e., skip copying an element if it would be moved to the same position.

Round 3: Update the size of the array after processing to exactly match the number of retained elements, ensuring any leftover elements beyond the new size are effectively discarded and not accessible in subsequent operations.

